    narr:narration """This position disentangles three orthogonal ways of classifying a single user, converging on one case. The diagnosis names [a typology that conflated AI-fluency with distribution-motion](narr:Expr_2RealTessChatWidget20260423_39), corrected to read her [work-motion archetype as a packager type](narr:Expr_2RealTessChatWidget20260423_38). Commercial status is separated as [a relational arrangement rather than a sales-validated pricing call](narr:Expr_2RealTessChatWidget20260423_45), with the owner stating plainly [her tier placement rests on relationship, not sales targeting](narr:Expr_2RealTessChatWidget20260423_44) — and her business role is named as [the company's highest-volume feedback source](narr:Expr_2RealTessChatWidget20260423_54). Pricing evidence is bounded both ways: [she cannot exemplify Individual-tier payment behavior](narr:Expr_2RealTessChatWidget20260423_49), yet [her non-payment doesn't undercut Professional-tier pricing either](narr:Expr_2RealTessChatWidget20260423_50). The synthesis holds all three together in [one frame naming archetype, commercial status, and role separately](narr:Expr_2RealTessChatWidget20260423_47). A separate thread asks [whether a given outreach channel suits her cohort](narr:Expr_3RealChannelNotProduct20260428_26), placing her as [a canonical example within a differently-named consumer archetype where the barrier is technical rather than behavioral](narr:Expr_3RealChannelNotProduct20260428_29).""" ;
